# 6. TCP Communication Modes


## Mode 1: Persistent Connection


In persistent mode:

The TCP connection is created only once.


Workflow: TCP Three Way Handshake 
Send Message 1

Receive ACK

Send Message 2

Receive ACK

.....

Send Message 10

Receive ACK



Advantages:


- Less overhead
- Faster communication
- Suitable for continuous communication


Examples:

- Chat applications
- File transfer
- Streaming applications


---

# Mode 2: New Connection Per Message


In this mode:

A new TCP connection is created for every message.


Workflow:
Handshake

 |

Send Message

 |

Receive ACK

 |

Close Connection

Repeat 10 times


Advantages:

- Simple implementation
- Suitable for short communication


Disadvantages:

- More handshake overhead
- Higher delay



Examples:

- Short API requests
- One-time services



---

# 7. Message Format


Client sends: MSG_ID|MESSAGE_SIZE|MESSAGE_DATA



Example: 3|512|AAAAAAAAAAAA


Server replies: ACK|MSG_ID|RECEIVED_SIZE


Example: ACK|3|512

